# Keeps the Docker build context (repo root — see infra/docker-compose.yml
# `build.context: ..`) from shadowing what the *container's own* pnpm
# install produces.
#
# This is load-bearing, not tidiness: infra/docker/api.Dockerfile's `build`
# stage does `COPY apps/api apps/api` after the `deps` stage already ran
# `pnpm install` inside the image. Without this file, that COPY would
# overwrite the container's freshly-installed, Linux-native
# `apps/api/node_modules` with whatever happens to be sitting in the local
# working tree on the machine running `docker build` — platform-specific
# binaries and pnpm's symlink layout included. Anyone building this image
# from a checkout with `node_modules` already installed locally (the normal
# state of a working tree) hits this.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
coverage
**/coverage
.git
.expo
*.log
openapi.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
